    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0736" n="620" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg620"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003 C 73/41</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Chargé</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Yung
                        Kwai</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-05-04"><hi rendition="#italic">May 4,
                        1923</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous oral exchange of
                    views regarding the time and place for the meeting of the Commission to
                    investigate and report upon extraterritoriality and administration of justice in
                    China as provided in a Resolution adopted by the Washington Conference, I have
                    the honor to inform you that my Government will be pleased to have the
                    Commission meet at Peking on November 1st, 1923.</p>
                <pb facs="0737" n="621" xml:id="pg621"/>
                <p>Moreover, I am instructed to request that you will be so kind as to send formal
                    notifications to the Governments of all the interested Powers with regard to the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Yung Kwai</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
